# Build-time system packages for lunchbox-launcher
# These are required to compile the Rust code
# One package per line, comments start with #

# Core build tools
build-essential
pkg-config

# GLib/GTK development libraries
libglib2.0-dev
libgtk-4-dev
libadwaita-1-dev
libcairo2-dev
libpango1.0-dev
libgdk-pixbuf-xlib-2.0-dev

# Wayland development libraries
libwayland-dev
libxkbcommon-dev
libudev-dev

# X11 (for XWayland support)
libx11-dev

# GObject introspection
libgirepository1.0-dev

# Layer shell for HUD overlay
libgtk4-layer-shell-dev

# LLVM toolchain.
#
# NOT for bpf-linker, despite what this comment used to claim: it is
# pinned to a release whose default `rust-llvm-*` feature links through
# rustc's own bundled LLVM (see BPF_LINKER_VERSION in scripts/lib/deps.sh),
# so it builds with no system LLVM present and ignores these entirely.
# Verified by installing it with these packages absent from the search
# path and no LLVM_* variable set.
#
# They are kept because `clang` is a generally-assumed build tool and the
# -dev packages are cheap insurance for any crate that grows a bindgen or
# llvm-sys dependency; if you are trimming the CI image, these are
# candidates, but drop them behind a green firewall-BPF build rather than
# on the strength of this note.
clang
llvm-20-dev
libpolly-20-dev

# libmpv (used by lunchbox-media for in-process media playback)
libmpv-dev

# D-Bus client library (required by bluer, the BLE transport in
# lunchbox-ble; bluer talks to BlueZ over the system bus).
libdbus-1-dev

# Required for rustup
curl

# Node.js / npm (required to build the embedded web UI before cargo build)
npm
